    affiliation: "Faculty of Information Technology, Czech Technical University in Prague"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarekSuchanek/vizbind"
abstract: >-
  VizBind is a declarative RDF vocabulary that describes an ontology visual
  notation as data rather than as tool code. A notation is a set of binding
  rules, each separating selection of model constructs (via SPARQL), mapping to
  abstract visual constructs, and engine-agnostic styling, with priority-based
  conflict resolution. The same RDFS/OWL model renders into different notations
  by swapping one file, and the same notation renders through different engines.
  This repository contains the vocabulary, two notations (a VOWL subset and a
  contrasting UML-style notation), a proof-of-concept Python engine with
  Graphviz, Mermaid and Cytoscape.js adapters, and the evaluation scripts that
  generate every figure and number reported in the accompanying paper.
keywords:
  - ontology visualization
  - visual notation
  - RDF
  - OWL
  - RDFS
  - SPARQL
